{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '505,575p' src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc; sed -n '2100,2145p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'float-address-test|test-ns|test/yang|antlr.*test' bb.edn test src/cljs | head -40; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc | sed -n '236,255p;345,360p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc | sed -n '872,890p'; rg -n 'scalar\\\\?|float64|decode-value|decode-scalar' src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   ['callable? [1] callable?]])\n\n\n(defn- arity-checked\n  \"`f` refusing, as data, a call whose argument count `arities` does not\n   admit, so a wrong count never reaches a host arity exception.\"\n  [op arities f]\n  (let [fixed (set (filter number? arities))\n        variadic-from (when (some #{:variadic} arities) (apply max fixed))]\n    (fn [& args]\n      (let [n (count args)]\n        (when-not (or (contains? fixed n)\n                      (and variadic-from (>= n variadic-from)))\n          (refuse! op :arity {::argc n}))\n        (apply f args)))))\n\n\n(def data-module\n  \"The `data` module's exports, export symbol to host function.\"\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[op arities f]] [op (arity-checked op arities f)]))\n        exports))\n\n\n(def data-profiles\n  \"UCF 7.5.2 profiles for the `data` module: every export `:pure`,\n   declaring no effects and no host state.\"\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[op arities _]]\n               [op (vm/primitive-profile op :pure arities #{} :none)]))\n        exports))\n\n\n(defn register-data-module\n  \"Return registry with the `data` module installed. Composition-only:\n   the module is never in `yin.vm/primitives`.\"\n  [registry]\n  (module/register-host-module registry module-name data-module\n                               data-profiles))\nnot consume `hash()`; they use the keys above. `hash()` of an identity\nobject (generator, instance, function) is unsupported in C3, since the\nonly available identity is the cell id, which is not exposed and not\nstable across lift.\n\nInteger `is` is value-based through the unchanged `py/is`, which stays\n`(= a b)` and is carrier-independent by ruling 2; this matches section\n8.11's \"same type and value\" rule (ruling 8). `True is 1` stays false.\nNo CPython allocation or interning fidelity is promised.\n\nNumeric limits are explicit Python-profile data in bits and digits, with\nno implicit default and nothing inherited from environment variables or\nhost library defaults (ruling 11). A bit-length breach is a guest\n`MemoryError` and a digit-limit breach is a guest `ValueError`, both\ncatchable and deterministic; neither is `OverflowError`. Real host\nexhaustion, timeout, and cancellation stay operational (section 11).\nCalling a large synchronous kernel `:pure` does not make it\ninterruptible, so C3 makes no mid-primitive safepoint or latency claim.\n\nThe stream codec is not widened and C3 builds no new adapter (ruling\n12). A raw remote put of a bignum refuses with a qualified outcome;\ncanonical Jing bytes through the existing `dao.jing.stream` adapter are\nthe only remote form, and printing and re-reading EDN is not a bignum\ntransport. NaN key identity and full float rendering parity remain\nseparately tracked limitations, not claimed by C3 (ruling 13).\n\n```text\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Slice  | Scope                                                               |\n+========+=====================================================================+\n| S0     | Freeze contracts: profile, expected bytes, literals, hashes,        |\n|        | outcomes, and boundary values around 2^53, 2^63, and 2^64. No       |\n|        | existing canonical fixture changes.                                 |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| S1     | Exact carriers and the pure module, installed explicitly; a         |\n|        | registry without it refuses.                                        |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| S2     | Literal and boundary integration: equal spellings give equal rows,  |\n|        | bytes, and hashes; malformed encodings refuse.                      |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| S3     | Integer operators, including augmented forms, through the prelude;  |\n|        | every C1 arithmetic regression still passes.                        |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| S4     | Conversions and comparisons: float bits, exact text, tagged float   |\n|        | results, exceptions; no double rounding.                            |\n+--------+---------------------------------------------------------------------+\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/safepoint_test.cljc:13:    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :refer [packet]]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.e2e-c1-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj:3:   through the same stream topology as `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test`:\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c1_test.clj:8:    [yang.python.antlr.e2e-test :as e2e]))\ntest/yang/python/antlr/scope_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.scope-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.prelude-parity-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.float-address-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc:17:    [yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test :refer [packet]]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.e2e-c2-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:4:   `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test`. Expected output is CPython 3.9.6's for the\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_c2_test.clj:9:    [yang.python.antlr.e2e-test :as e2e]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.e2e-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.lower-portable-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/lower_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.lower-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/cst_export_test.clj:1:(ns yang.python.antlr.cst-export-test\n   236\t   :cljs through a DataView with littleEndian explicitly true, :cljd\n   237\t   through a big-endian ByteData store read in reverse. On :cljs the\n   238\t   float64 carrier is unwrapped first: a DataView coerces an object\n   239\t   through its text, which loses -0.0's sign.\"\n   240\t  [x]\n   241\t  (let [v #?(:cljs (if (number? x) x (.-v ^not-native x)) :default x)]\n   242\t    (if (not= v v)\n   243\t      \"000000000000f87f\"\n   244\t      #?(:clj (int64-le-hex (Double/doubleToLongBits (double v)))\n   245\t         :cljs (let [view (js/DataView. (js/ArrayBuffer. 8))]\n   246\t                 (.setFloat64 view 0 v true)\n   247\t                 (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 view %) 2) (range 8))))\n   248\t         :cljd (let [bd (ByteData. 8)]\n   249\t                 (.setFloat64 bd 0 v)\n   250\t                 (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 bd %) 2) (range 7 -1 -1))))))))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t;; =============================================================================\n   254\t;; Host scalar classification (S2 item 4)\n   255\t;; =============================================================================\n   345\t   bigint, not a long by this host's own rule -- CLJS has no BigDecimal/\n   346\t   Float distinction from a plain number to lose, so the complement rule\n   347\t   stays correct there. Jing's float64 carrier, how JS keeps an integral\n   348\t   float's kind, is :double too.\"\n   349\t  [v]\n   350\t  #?(:clj (instance? Double v)\n   351\t     :default (or (and (cbor/float64? v) (not (number? v)))\n   352\t                  (and (number? v) (not (host-long? v)) (not (host-ratio? v))\n   353\t                       (not (host-bigint? v))))))\n   354\t\n   355\t\n   356\t(defn scalar-class\n   357\t  \"Classify `v` under this dimension's own S2 scalar domain: the class\n   358\t   keyword when `v` is representable, nil when it is not. Recursive over\n   359\t   vectors, lists, maps, and sets -- a collection classifies only when\n   360\t   every element does. No normalization and no folding of any kind\n   872\t   reverse — the endianness is stated, never the platform's default. On\n   873\t   :cljs the float64 carrier is unwrapped first: a DataView coerces an\n   874\t   object through its text, which loses -0.0's sign.\"\n   875\t  [x]\n   876\t  (let [v #?(:cljs (if (number? x) x (.-v ^not-native x)) :default x)]\n   877\t    (if (not= v v)\n   878\t      \"000000000000f87f\"\n   879\t      #?(:clj (int64-le-hex (Double/doubleToLongBits (double v)))\n   880\t         :cljs (let [view (js/DataView. (js/ArrayBuffer. 8))]\n   881\t                 (.setFloat64 view 0 v true)\n   882\t                 (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 view %) 2) (range 8))))\n   883\t         :cljd (let [bd (ByteData. 8)]\n   884\t                 (.setFloat64 bd 0 v)\n   885\t                 (apply str (map #(to-hex (.getUint8 bd %) 2) (range 7 -1 -1))))))))\n   886\t\n   887\t\n   888\t(defn- ident-content\n   889\t  \"§5 keywords and symbols encode namespace and name separately, each\n   890\t   through the NFC seam — the value table declares :nfc-utf-8 for both\n633:(defn- scalar?\n637:   answers false to `number?` (C3 ruling 4), and so is Jing's float64\n641:      (cbor/float64? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x)))\n713:              (scalar? x) x\n1957:          (if (or (scalar? x) (contains? seen entry))\n2064:  (if (or (scalar? v) (empty? (:heap state)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
