{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '1247,1276p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc | sed -n '77,85p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '1951,1965p;2058,2071p'; nl -ba test/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc | sed -n '299,317p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1247\trecords the C3 integer rulings.\n  1248\t\n  1249\tFloat kind before addresses (float-address mob ruling). Every\n  1250\tfloating-point value entering canonical rows or an addressed image,\n  1251\tincluding prelude constants, nested Python float payloads, and runtime\n  1252\tfloats held in snapshots, continuations, and heap entries, must preserve\n  1253\tfloat64 kind before host representation erases it. Addressed values use\n  1254\tJing's existing float64 representation (`dao.jing.cbor/float64`, the\n  1255\tcarrier on JavaScript). A Python float wrapper alone does not establish\n  1256\tthe numeric kind of its payload. Row projection and transformation must\n  1257\tpreserve that kind. Concretely: the lowering builds `{:py/float\n  1258\t(float64 x)}` while the literal syntax still says float; the prelude's\n  1259\t`py/float` wraps through `data/float64` and `py/num` unwraps through\n  1260\t`data/float-value`, with host arithmetic on bare numbers in between; the\n  1261\tquoted prelude holds no integral float literal (JavaScript reads `1.0` as\n  1262\t`1` before any code runs), and every float constant reaches arithmetic as\n  1263\tan operand of `data/float-value`, which is also the bridge back from a\n  1264\tcarrier decoded out of a row. A normalized numeric dict or set key is the\n  1265\tinteger when integral within +/-(2^53 - 1), so `1`, `1.0`, `True` and\n  1266\t`-0.0`/`0` key alike, and float64 content otherwise. The VM admits the\n  1267\tcarrier as a scalar at `plain-data?`, `machine-data?` and the lift and\n  1268\tpin `scalar?` gate. The JVM goldens in\n  1269\t`test